<title>USA: Fannie Mae increases size of SMBS trust 276.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae increases size of SMBS trust 276.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae said it increased the size of Strip Mortgage-Backed Securities (SMBS) trust 276 to $360 million from $300 million.</p>
<p>The deal, issued via Nomura Securities International Inc, has a new settlement date of February 28, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>It has a weighted average coupon of 7.06 percent, a weighted average maturity of 311 months and a PSA-estimated prepayment speed of 100, the agency said.</p>
<p>The issue is backed by 30-year 6.5-percent single-family fixed-rate mortgages.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
